  "notes": "Each Warren precinct had one contest, 'Member of Warren County Republican Committee <precinct>', vote for 2 (no gender split). A seat is 'filled' when a printed ballot candidate received votes, 'empty' when no candidate ran and zero write-in votes were cast, and 'unknown' when write-in votes were cast, since the report does not show whether a write-in winner qualified or accepted. The separate precinct-level PDF (DocumentCenter/View/3836, about 55 MB) was not needed because the summary already reports each precinct's committee contest. Appointments after the primary are not reflected. Holder names come from the official results export: on each seat already counted as filled, the winning ballot candidate as printed (named write-ins are never used)."
